    "body": "## Motivation\n\nDeepSeek-V4 NPU prefill builds compressed RoPE positions separately for each request and compression ratio. It currently creates consecutive group IDs with `arange`, then multiplies the tensor by 4 or 128.\n\nGenerate the positions directly with a stepped `arange`. This removes the extra multiplication and its intermediate tensor for each nonempty request/ratio pair, keeping the same int64 positions and padding.\n\n## Validation\n\n297 cases passed on CPU and Ascend NPU using the actual prefill helper and an independent position oracle. Covers C4/C128, prefix and compression boundaries, empty queries and empty batches.\n\nHelper microbenchmark on one Ascend NPU, approximately 4,096 query tokens per request:\n\n| Batch | Before | After |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | 0.331 ms | 0.295 ms |\n| 8 | 0.690 ms | 0.447 ms |\n| 32 | 1.972 ms | 1.036 ms |\n\nABBA order, each arm with 5 warmups and 3 groups of 20 calls, synchronized at group boundaries. These are prefill metadata helper timings, not model TTFT/TPOT. Both arms use the same main source and retain the original CPU readback; #47663 is not stacked here.\n\nFormatting and lint checks passed. Two Windows hooks could not launch `python3`; the same scripts passed with the available Python executable.\n\n[Reproduction scripts, frozen sources and raw results](https://github.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/tree/f1d7db04cea1eb539743914b543e2cf5fc01ed87) are on a separate evidence branch. No test files are added to this PR.\n\nReport generated from the recorded results:\n\n![Validation and helper benchmark](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/f1d7db04cea1eb539743914b543e2cf5fc01ed87/validation.png)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41212230201](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41212230201)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41212230183](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41212230183)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41212230148](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41212230148)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
